'Gemini Decision 1 [repeat 1]' plays its 17 required original pairs (league #26: #993-#999, #1005, #1013,
#1053, #1055-#1057, #1060-#1063) pinned to each original match's seed and seating, the same option-order seed
(1190975713392774006), bg-v2, League 1 rules (3 rounds, 300 turns, mirror_concurrent) and settings (OpenRouter
System One route google/gemini-decision-1, provider only google-ai-studio, fallbacks off; only name and note change).
GPT-6 Luna (never scheduled) and Mercury Decide (#1016 aborted at its start, no game) are not required (Ümit #5220):
recorded under coverage_required.not_required, not pinned. coverage_required counts separately: required 17,
history_played 17, pinned 17, playable_today 17, matched_fixtures 17.

Runner: RUNNER_GEMINI = branch pinned-late-gemini cb669a0 (0e66836 + dab6da5, 1b234da, c0b58f3, 38024d6
cherry-picked: the `request` merge, map-check v2, raw_entries), binary 0bf67bc3..., tree
~/code/jevgammon-runner-gemini, the 18 build inputs unchanged; bound by check as RUNNER is (per-repeat runner,
already read from the manifest; attempts() now records each repeat's own runner).
Cap: the original's $5 entry cap, $1.1819 recorded by its guard, so the repeat's guard stops at $3.8181 (cap_usd,
cap_basis); billed_usd counts a hosted entrant's own cost by server kind (api), unchanged for d1-ultra.
GPU: hosted entrant; the 8 local opponents run on a second card (start command OPP_GPU=<second card>).
Smoke: the original's listed() check (OpenRouter lists one endpoint, google-ai-studio, up, $0.10/$0).
Per-repeat options (prepared, requested_by, not_required, cap_usd/cap_basis, opp_gpu, concurrency) default to
the six existing entries' values; start commands name this launcher's run.sh.

Manifest: the Gemini entry appended from `repeats.py manifest` on 2026-11-12 (v3.db read-only); the six other
entries and the top level are kept as committed (a full regeneration would only add their now-created leagues
to attempts and this launcher's path to start). leagues/gemini-decision-1-r1.json from `repeats.py configs` (the
six other configs byte-identical).

test_launcher: each runner a repeat binds is cloned and copied (runner/, runner-<commit>/); Gemini's name is not
held in main yet, so it refuses on that alone, then runs the trigger-missing case with its case's repeats.py
reading a scratch main that holds it (check 3, prepared, check 0 with its 18 clients admitted by cb669a0);
its entrant without the provider pin and the 0e66836 binary in its place each refuse. 70 ok, ALL PASSED.
